{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:5c9af6360e1b4de863bba74fd0a1f8d408efa7cadd36ad6f46b6dad86db66a4b","title":"The setting isolates geometrical effects of averaging ordinary gravitating matter. It removes local pressure and rotational support so that positive regional acceleration, if obtained with zero cosmological constant, must come from the averaging terms.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0002"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c2572fb5ac4d8164d8608d971866a2cfe81b455b1af43cf8bc57636d9f25636","title":"Must the particular extremal repulson singularities survive as physical configurations and receive a quantum resolution? The paper motivates this through supersymmetry and known string examples, while distinguishing classical solutions from demonstrated quantum states.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0006"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c90bbd38b0b2c152f80fa1290e8a29d15fcd0a9f40d23ef31ac76bd1f3cce47","title":"How can modified gravitational theories differ observably from GR and from one another while satisfying established gravitational tests, and can their cosmology address dark matter, acceleration or the cosmological constant problem?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0011"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5cd1d3cca171c64dd57fe4adae61dd048756d13f04237d7a3774931728a6f0c8","title":"What scalar non-Gaussianity and tensor spectra arise when gauge-field production supplies the friction needed for inflation on a steep axion potential? Can low-energy inflation produce observable chiral tensors?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0012"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c474dddabd28af3a6559a75af32bff50241b635118305fd32955733b719c62c","title":"Can perturbative α′ corrections alone generate a small nonzero cosmological constant in controlled heterotic compactifications at string tree level, once higher external-curvature terms beyond an effective scalar potential are retained?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0012"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c57d59057069b1b90c14541005c44710d3ff3e04d6481d6499fde71bc400e1b","title":"How does lattice choice, equivalently structure-constant quantization, determine whether a flat-group Scherk–Schwarz compactification genuinely breaks supersymmetry and lifts moduli, and whether its left-invariant truncation describes the low-energy spectrum?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0014"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c152fe740d9a523ec605164885e60207967c191775f9f3b4faf38ef1e0b0a9f","title":"Does the inflationary attractor of conformally coupled models survive general negative nonminimal coupling ξ, and what explains the rapid convergence of scalar tilt and tensor predictions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0014"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c497e6fd82091d7773d87faa5b46919398f100c880cac7f0907b56688d3a775","title":"Can classical type IIB supergravity with O5/O7 sources produce supersymmetric AdS4 compactifications admitting weak coupling, large internal volume, and an AdS radius parametrically larger than the compactification scale?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0014"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5cdd15b8390a7af6b046c482c7c8548310c6cf068c83bee78b85fdbca6874a8b","title":"How can conformal symmetry, unitarity and OPE consistency constrain strongly coupled CFTs without choosing a microscopic Lagrangian? These pedagogical lectures develop the foundations and introduce numerical applications to the 2d and 3d Ising models.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0021"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c2fb8c90799014c942acc69e6cda99251764b067e00463763c3d626aa4bfe70","title":"Can GR be formulated using a flat, torsion-free affine geometry with a removable connection and a boundary-term-free gravitational action, and can this formulation provide simple modified-gravity cosmologies?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0026"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c62117de477890a3cfd2382a6577cd191e4356d2a4db659ea788b43709d64ad","title":"Which effective theories can arise from string compactification, and how can compactification geometries, gauge bundles and their simultaneous moduli be constructed, constrained and counted?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0028"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c4dec2666af6de3b814de6b1e375eabdc68397ae11e2af235e2a418612bba62","title":"Do conjectured restrictions on field distance and potential steepness exclude inflation, or can a non-geodesic trajectory sustain slow expansion despite a steep total potential gradient?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0030"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5cc0fbc343c071e6efca8e63f802682196609fccdf01074e9e2bbd2938c0320f","title":"What replaces a six-dimensional gauge theory as its gauge coupling vanishes at fixed gravitational strength? The paper studies wrapped D3-brane strings and their charged excitations along this Kähler-moduli limit.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0031"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c500ad9ce3afc70c48fb0ef34b15135f44412ac13a49fceab100dad55498174","title":"Can a tower of non-BPS string excitations satisfy the precise charge-to-mass bound determined by both gravity and massless scalars, including in theories with several abelian gauge fields?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0034"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c04c1ac4f9fb9f4dfa69d3baada4babb48ea9296747de7160cfacc9af55ea23","title":"How are multifield inflationary paths and their ordinary field excursions defined? Homogeneous fields evolve under a potential with Hubble friction on a curved, positive-definite target space.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0034"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5cc4241154011779081b88cf058ecf848a0124c40bfc55408efcb05e19350069","title":"Can interactions with light fields sustain inflation while transferring energy to radiation? The source represents this possibility through an enhanced friction term in the homogeneous inflaton equation.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0038"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c7a05a1e1731cf6364e7a0aa96551d97489f2a5e03c2da2e0d10ccdf7678592","title":"Can consistency of strings coupled to tensor fields impose a finite upper bound on independent U(1) gauge factors in six-dimensional N=(1,0) quantum gravity, including theories with non-abelian sectors?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0042"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5ca4d1a302b499ae39c0892ef5e9d74bdd5f1272ad93602da3b581789c265f24","title":"How does a landscape with many more terminal than inflating minima differ from the usual multiverse landscape?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0045"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5cbd446db33069c6cbf26f3a2d9087ae29e03f14dde2500a93d1c5d36fe0c825","title":"Can nonminimal coupling to gravity improve matrix inflation's observational predictions, reduce the required D3-brane multiplicity, enable spectator preheating and alleviate excursions beyond the proposed UV cutoff?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0045"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c013c1524883fb8b01545ead9ba123903d6efe8327b3440a46c6772965f447a","title":"Can different quantum-gravity modifications of scalar and tensor perturbations suppress their power ratio in single-field inflation subject to an order-one lower bound on the potential gradient?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0048"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c27c5570c104f867a0d5b17ea1433a98a4e7906eebbc859cd629c704fbeec05","title":"Does massive IIA O6-core resolution preserve the low-energy spectrum and hierarchy inferred from bulk supergravity? What next-order Kähler data and internal geometric structure describe the localized vacua?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0050"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5cd6d4b2b223541287d05e896f5e0f4be1f14576d361ba0add5238fe2c8e4c07","title":"What response does a comoving pointlike Unruh–DeWitt detector have when quadratically coupled to a complex scalar in de Sitter spacetime, and how do regularization, massless minimal coupling, and α-vacuum choice affect its interpretation?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0051"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5cc28a434c78cb9d597bb1d3937e978274055222087a52156319811b69042491","title":"Which gravitational systems should obey the proposed one-state condition? The paper distinguishes complete higher-dimensional quantum gravity from low-dimensional worldsheet or topological descriptions, where familiar restrictions on parameters, symmetries, and cobordism may fail.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0051"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c57793bfe2b69a7f10cae45744159a7be7ab72d459445d1bd3d622a3abc0c5a","title":"Which physical processes threaten weak or strong cosmic censorship, how should generic initial conditions be defined, and can semiclassical or quantum effects preserve predictability?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0052"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c0c88decfc007e9bc0464d8334f804b47598f869924ab1895bfe9c3b2cd900d","title":"Can CFT consistency require a heavy tower rather than constrain its couplings after its existence is assumed? The source identifies this existence problem as a distinct missing part of the proposed distance-conjecture connection.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0053"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c9426614ef244329bda294e21a71dcc46e6558868643d1240df2eb1dce7cb13","title":"Could conjecturally short inflationary vacuum lifetimes motivate observable transitions between inflationary stages?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0057"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c10d5f1d2a09d04db45a30e88f1bb8b875769743ea19767b4696b92ae6ce2ae","title":"Can mobile space-filling branes coexist with stuck probes under one orientifold? The shifted construction separates the space-filling twisted-tadpole requirement from the allowed charge of a lower-dimensional probe.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0058"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c3940f5818efe27497c6487485921e29a481504458e4f1bd7ecc94ed38e785e","title":"How do PBH formation, evolution, clustering and binary formation determine gravitational-wave signatures, distinguish primordial from stellar black holes, and enable detection with LISA?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0084"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5ca7064ae31682db041cf5efcee0facf64c6fa34b6ded58f9d261158c334d8c2","title":"How do simultaneous charge and rotation affect braneworld quantum-black-hole thermodynamics, criticality, semiclassical validity, quantum inequalities and the gyromagnetic ratio?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0095"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c38d79a2d6372469a8073ae3038bf43ddf146e847d471ee39ea85595b1299b6","title":"How do infinite-distance taxonomy relations constrain commutators in moduli-space quantum mechanics, and can moduli-space geometry produce normalizable excited states localized away from classical runaway limits?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0099"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5cf714ff1e97c7ee299c92d53371e311e46daaa2d38bc9588b6216f097196124","title":"Why is vacuum energy so small, can dynamical dark energy reduce fine tuning or cosmic coincidence, and how can observations distinguish a cosmological constant from evolving quintessence?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0103"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c85851b79f0438ab83420ea87ab925ae233b4d9bd5a9890e6b4136e45397ded","title":"Can the weak-scale gravity framework with large extra dimensions be embedded in perturbative string theory, and what collider signatures and model-building requirements follow?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0107"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c510fc5d73a4522baed5d0c84950885a709422c9c6ada7fa9e675fdc1fc02f1","title":"Why is gravitational vacuum energy so small, with positive ΛL_P² ≈ 10^-123, and why is its density comparable to matter today? What can cosmological observations establish about its nature?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0109"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c0a7ebfa5b0fc1e9adfcdbc14f4190f282ff1a520ff9ad7b25e7103da7ccd0c","title":"Which bound orbits can a probe antibrane execute around source branes, when are fully relativistic trajectories closed and non-precessing, and how long can such systems survive bending and radiative instabilities?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0110"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c1c76e31b1bbdbfcb63cb79fbaf05187d3e1a1c0ac2c7b8bc199e99a44d6377","title":"How do string-theoretic forces stabilize moduli and produce cosmological vacua, what microphysical degrees of freedom account for their entropy, and how do velocity-dependent effects change moduli dynamics?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0111"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5cdd658eecd9f0a76a8e34b8b5b7e478cd447ec4647635e162fc70e239549a57","title":"Can a root-of-unity quantum deformation extend finite-dimensional, unitary dS/CFT constructions to three-dimensional de Sitter space, regulate horizon entanglement entropy, and relate representation parameters to the cosmological constant?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0111"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5cf4bfe89780749d93a6ef1bf7a1e56ae79e5e051f959a5fc05ea639814c2fba","title":"What bulk geometries describe the zero-temperature gauge-theory vacuum on S² × S¹, how does the preferred geometry depend on circle size, and is gravitational energy bounded below at fixed conformal boundary?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0115"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c65d0cc3602f62da727f036ccdefaed1719e834b500725b75902f372f9d3e66","title":"What is the leading α′ correction to the extremal magnetic GHS black hole's mass-charge relation, and how can it be extracted despite field-redefinition ambiguity in the higher-derivative effective action?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0118"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5c38dec44f67763f219e1d7c6746dfff153c7dab198f79d87f22e332ef331d77","title":"What controls string theories at st